TITLE:: WriteCommand
SUMMARY:: Command that writes the piano-roll pattern to the sequencer document.
CATEGORIES:: Commands
RELATED:: Classes/Command, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/SequencerDocument

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::WriteCommand:: is a LINK::Classes/Command:: that inserts dummy pattern text through LINK::Classes/SequencerDocument#-insertPattern::. It is constructed with an optional LINK::Classes/SequencerDocument:: (CODE::nil:: is allowed for scratchpad use). Loop bounds are LINK::Classes/Parameter::s named CODE::loopStart:: and CODE::loopEnd::; LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: supplies them through LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt#-ambientParameters::, so the user does not type them. After the CODE::write:: chip is committed, LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt:: treats the command as satisfied. Press Return to execute.

If the document is CODE::nil::, LINK::#-execute:: posts a warning and does nothing.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::WriteCommand::.

ARGUMENT:: sequencerDocument
An optional LINK::Classes/SequencerDocument:: to write into. Pass CODE::nil:: when no document is available.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::WriteCommand:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: execute
Inserts dummy pattern text including the given loop start, end, and length. Warns and returns if no document was provided at construction.

ARGUMENT:: args
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\loopStart:: and CODE::\loopEnd:: as LINK::Classes/Number::s.

PRIVATE:: prSetSequencerDocument
